//! Icefall: a glacial valley under snow, 420 by 280 m, the same for red (-x) and blue (+x): each side's base built into the mountain at its end, a hangar behind a concrete facade with three doors and a terrace on its roof where its flier stands, a forecourt between two spurs. Three ways across: the frozen lake to the north, open and fast, with a skerry in its middle and islets for cover; the moraine to the south, drumlins and snags and a snow shed along the wall; and between them a massif a side with a perch on its crest, the col between the two with the rocket on its station. A launcher at each door throws you a third of the way: to the perch, to the shore, to the first drumlin.
